Description: Nodes for survey sampling in a trama graph: sample size for means
    and proportions with finite population correction, design effect and
    non-response; stratified sample size with proportional, Neyman, cost
    optimal and equal allocation; cluster sample size from the intraclass
    correlation; selection of simple random, systematic, stratified,
    probability proportional to size, one-stage and two-stage cluster samples;
    declared designs and post-stratification; design-based estimation of
    means, totals, proportions and ratios, in domains, with the ultimate
    cluster variance estimator; and Monte Carlo simulation of a design against
    a known population. The selected sample carries its design, so estimation
    never asks for it again. Builds on trama.data for tables and trama.view
    for plots.
